icator. Pass non-interactive children or a selection-state\nrender function to replace the default circle and icon. See the Multiple selection example."],[1884,"`categoryColors` maps individual category values to palette color indices, overriding\nthe series color for just those bars — so a single series can carry a different color\nper category. All three periods here share the same category-to-color map, so each\nchannel keeps one color across every period; the comparison periods are dropped to\nreduced opacity."],[325,"`CheckboxGroup` is composed: write `Label`, a `Group` holding the `Checkbox` items, `Text slot=\"description\"`, and `FieldError`. The `Group` takes its axis, gap, and presentational role from the group's `orientation`, so a bare `<Group>` is all you need; pass your own `direction`/`gap` to lay the items out differently. Each `Checkbox` takes label text next to the indicator."],[395,"`ChipButton` for menu filters and other actions with a Chip-like appearance"],[413,"`ChipButton` is a real button and exposes menu state through `MenuTrigger`; provide an accessible name when the visible content is incomplete."],[391,"`ChipGroup` + `ChipList` + `Chip` for grouped values, selection, keyboard navigation, and removal"],[406,"`ChipGroup` owns selection and removal behavior. Use a Chip render prop for\nstate-dependent content, and `Button` with `slot=\"remove\"` together with\n`onRemove` for removable items. See **Toggle Chips** and **Removable Chips**."],[1821,"`className` and `style` apply to the tooltip panel."],[482,"`Collapsible`: `data-expanded`, `data-disabled`, and `data-focus-visible-within`."],[492,"`CollapsiblePanel` is labeled by its trigger through `aria-labelledby` automatically."],[493,"`CollapsiblePanel` uses `role=\"group\"` by default. Keep it when the panel's content does not need\na navigation landmark; there is no need to set it explicitly."],[484,"`CollapsiblePanel`: `data-focus-visible-within`."],[2041,"`colorIndex` pins each series t