ll to action, a second paragraph, an image — without the component\ngrowing a prop for it."],[1275,"`thumbNames` configures native form field names and does not provide accessible labels. Likewise, `valueLabel`, `minLabel`, and `maxLabel` are visual context rather than substitutes for accessible naming."],[959,"`titleInfo` requires `title` to be set — the info icon is contextually tied to the title label. If `title` is absent, `titleInfo` has no effect."],[1815,"`TooltipTrigger` wraps a focusable element and a `<Tooltip>`, handling hover/focus state and positioning automatically."],[2035,"`tooltipValueFormatter` shapes only the tooltip values, so you can show full currency or units there while the axis stays compact."],[960,"`trend` is intended to accompany `description` to provide temporal context (e.g. \"↑ +3% vs. last month\"). A trend icon alone, with no description, leaves the direction unanchored (\"up since *when*?\"). If `description` is not provided, `trend` has no effect."],[2045,"`variant` sets each series' line style — 'solid' (default), 'dashed', or\n'dotted' — useful for distinguishing actuals from forecasts or targets. The\nlegend swatch mirrors each line's style."],[2023,"`xBaseline` and `yBaseline` control the main axis lines themselves. Dropping them gives a lighter, more editorial chart."],[1878,"`xDomain` and `yDomain` pin down exactly which categories and value range to draw. Here category `F` has no data and still gets an empty slot, and the Y range stays `[0, 40]` even though the largest bar is 30 - handy when several charts need to share a scale."],[2028,"`xDomain` and `yDomain` pin the visible range. Use them to keep a fixed scale, or to keep several charts comparable."],[2019,"`xGridlines` and `yGridlines` add faint lines across the plot so it is easier to read a value back off an axis."],[2080,"`xl` - Extra large spacing"],[2021,"`xLabels` and `yLabels` toggle the tick labels on each axis. Turn them off for sparklines or when the surrounding UI already names the values."],[2029,"`xNice` and `yNice` round the domain out to friendlier numbers (e.g. 0.2 to 1.0), so ticks land on values people expect."],[2032,"`xPaddingOuter` and `yPaddingOuter` add breathing room at the ends of a band or point scale so the first and last values are not pinned to the edges."],[2076,"`xs` - Extra small spacing"],[1879,"`xTickFormat` and `yTickFormat` shape the axis labels - abbreviated dates on one axis, thousands separators on the other. The functions receive the raw accessor value, so they also cover currency, units, or percentages."],[2025,"`xTickFormat` and `yTickFormat` shape the axis labels - dates, currency, units, percentages - and the tooltip follows the same formatting."],[2022,"`xTickMarks` and `yTickMarks` draw the short lines at each tick value, which helps tie a label to its exact position on the axis."],[2020,"`xTitle` and `yTitle` label what each axis actually measures, e.g. \"Month\" and \"Temperature (°F)\"."],[2030,"`xZero` and `yZero` stretch the domain to include zero. Worth doing when the absolute size of the values matters, not just their movement."],[1915,"✅ Custom domains"],[1916,"✅ Design system alignment"],[1512,"✅ For binary on/off preferences (e.g. Wi-Fi, notifications, dark mode)"],[1782,"✅ For compact action grouping — related actions in space-constrained layouts (e.g. Undo / Redo, Zoom In / Out / Reset)"],[1781,"✅ For grouped contextual actions — two or more closely related actions that belong together (e.g. Bold / Italic / Underline, Align Left / Center / Right)"],[1783,"✅ For multi-select scenarios — when users need to select multiple options simultaneously"],[344,"✅ For selecting multiple independent options"],[1511,"✅ For settings that take effect immediately, without a form submission"],[346,"✅ For toggling settings or features on/off"],[1914,"✅ Interactive tooltips"],[1913,"✅ Responsive behavior with sticky axes"],[1911,"✅ Single and multi-series support"],[1912,"✅ Vertical and horizontal orientations"],[347,"✅ When all available options should be visible"],[1224,"✅ When all options should be visible at once"],[1225,"✅ When the decision is important and deserves space"],[1223,"✅ When there are 2-7 mutually exclusive options"],[345,"✅ When users can select zero, one, or many items"],[1227,"❌ For binary yes/no choices (use Checkbox or Toggle instead)"],[1514,"❌ For choosing one of several mutually exclusive options (use `Radio` or `SegmentedController` instead)"],[1785,"❌ For more than 5 choices — cognitive overload; consider a **Select** instead"],[1226,"❌ For more than 7 options (use Select instead)"],[1788,"❌ For mutually exclusive content views (e.g. Monthly / Yearly) — use **SegmentedController** instead"],[348,"❌ For mutually exclusive options (use Radio instead)"],[1513,"❌ For selections that require a \"Save\" or \"Submit\" action (use `Checkbox` instead)"],[349,"❌ For simple on/off toggles without labels (use Toggle/Switch instead)"],[1784,"❌ For unrelated actions that perform disconnected tasks without shared context"],[1786,"❌ When actions require strong visual distinction (e.g. Save vs. Delete)"],[1787,"❌ When selecting an option leads to a different page or workflow — use navigation instead"],[1228,"❌ When space is limited (use Select dropdown)"],[1919,"🚧 Additional customization options (tick formatting, axis configuration)"],[1917,"🚧 RTL compatibility (axis rendering and spacing refinement)"],[1918,"🚧 Tick mark positioning improvements"],[836,"A `<Button slot=\"trigger\">` gets `aria-expanded` + `aria-controls` wired to the `InlineDrawerPanel` automatically (via RAC Disclosure)."],[255,"A `CardGroup` does not submit form values. Read the selection from `onSelectionChange`."],[252,"A `CardGroup` is a grid: each Card is a row, Tab moves into and out of the group, and arrow keys\nmove between Cards. Name the group with `aria-label` or `aria-labelledby`. Each Card takes its\naccessible name from `textValue`, which also drives typeahead.